// Hakuro posed by the old code, held against the same pose here. The literals are what
// rywible/wrela at 7ae6711e made of him posed by `PALETTE`: every vertex of his left arm's
// level-0 grid (its place, as the old `chart::place_of(v, 0, band)` gave it, and the old
// `Limb::side` there), and each of his 27 parts at 4 places along its band by 6 round. They
// were written by a scratch tool run on the old toolchain, and are made again with
//
//     cd /Users/ryanwible/projects/wrela-notes/next/scratch/bodies/old
//     ~/.wrela/toolchains/0.33.0/bin/wrela tool tools/forms-place > ../forms/old_pose.txt
//
// then old_pose_file.py in /Users/ryanwible/projects/wrela-notes/next/scratch/bodies/forms,
// which writes this file from that output. The pose (the tool's `palette`): every bone turned
// a little about its own joint, a fixed spread of axes and angles; his left upper arm lowered
// 1.1 rad and turned 0.6 about its length, his left elbow bent 1.6 rad (so it folds) and his
// forearm turned 0.8 about its length, his right knee bent 1.3 rad; each matrix its parent's
// times its own turn. A point here is held within `WITHIN` of the old one.

use form::kinds::Chart
use hakuro::{
    CHARTS, WIDE_CHARTS, WRAP_TUCK, arms_through_coat, charted_as, charted_at_rest,
    jacket_body_cover,
}
use std::derive::{Box2, Box3}
use std::math::TAU

